.TH HIFIBERRY-EQ 1 "August 2025" "HiFiBerry PipeWire" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hifiberry-eq \- control HiFiBerry 16-band parametric equalizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hifiberry-eq
.B set-band
.I band type freq q gain
.br
.B hifiberry-eq
.B disable-band
.I band
.br
.B hifiberry-eq
.B reset
.br
.B hifiberry-eq
.B show
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hifiberry-eq
controls the 16-band parametric equalizer that is automatically inserted
into the HiFiBerry PipeWire audio pipeline. The EQ provides professional-grade
biquad filters for precise audio shaping.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "set-band " "band type freq q gain"
Configure a specific EQ band.
.I band
is 1-16,
.I type
is the filter type,
.I freq
is frequency in Hz,
.I q
is the Q factor (0.1-30.0),
.I gain
is gain in dB (-20.0 to +20.0).
.TP
.BI "disable-band " band
Disable a specific band (set to passthrough). Band number is 1-16.
.TP
.B reset
Reset all bands to passthrough, effectively disabling the EQ.
.TP
.B show
Show current EQ settings and filter node information.
.SH FILTER TYPES
.TP
.B lowpass
Low-pass filter (attenuates frequencies above cutoff)
.TP
.B highpass
High-pass filter (attenuates frequencies below cutoff)
.TP
.B bandpass
Band-pass filter (passes frequencies around cutoff)
.TP
.B lowshelf
Low-shelf filter (boost/cut low frequencies)
.TP
.B highshelf
High-shelf filter (boost/cut high frequencies)
.TP
.B peaking
Peaking filter (boost/cut around specific frequency)
.TP
.B notch
Notch filter (narrow attenuation at specific frequency)
.TP
.B allpass
All-pass filter (phase adjustment without amplitude change)
.TP
.B none
Disable filter (passthrough)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B hifiberry-eq set-band 1 highpass 80 0.7 0
Set band 1 as high-pass filter at 80Hz with Q=0.7
.TP
.B hifiberry-eq set-band 5 peaking 1000 2.0 3.5
Set band 5 to boost 1kHz by 3.5dB with Q=2.0
.TP
.B hifiberry-eq set-band 10 lowpass 8000 1.0 0
Set band 10 as low-pass filter at 8kHz
.TP
.B hifiberry-eq disable-band 3
Disable band 3 (set to passthrough)
.TP
.B hifiberry-eq reset
Reset all bands to passthrough
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/51-hifiberry-eq.conf
WirePlumber configuration that creates the 16-band EQ filter
